WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.583 --> 00:00:07.009
Welcome to CyberQuest, a cyber-safety learning platform for New Zealand schools.

2
00:00:08.383 --> 00:00:13.832
The home page starts with the problem: children are born online, but not born safe.

3
00:00:14.950 --> 00:00:19.134
It shows real New Zealand numbers, with the source under each one.

4
00:00:20.183 --> 00:00:26.770
It also explains New Zealand cyber law in simple words, like the Harmful Digital Communications Act.

5
00:00:28.617 --> 00:00:33.974
Pricing is fair. Every school can start with a free trial, and Level 1 is always free.

6
00:00:35.083 --> 00:00:40.962
Kura and small rural schools get a 50% community discount, shown in the last column.

7
00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:49.226
Now we log in as Tama, a Year 7 student.

8
00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:56.566
His dashboard shows his trail to the summit: six levels, from Year 7 to adult learners.

9
00:00:57.583 --> 00:01:02.185
He has passed Levels 1 and 2, and Level 3 is now open.

10
00:01:04.083 --> 00:01:09.916
Each level has three steps. First, he studies short topics with Kiwi examples.

11
00:01:11.150 --> 00:01:15.763
Then he practises, and when he is ready, he sits the level exam.

12
00:01:17.350 --> 00:01:21.418
In practice mode, Tama answers one question at a time.

13
00:01:22.983 --> 00:01:26.041
He picks an answer and presses Check my answer.

14
00:01:27.517 --> 00:01:31.689
The feedback is instant and kind. It never says Fail.

15
00:01:32.983 --> 00:01:36.552
It always shows the safe answer and explains why.

16
00:01:38.217 --> 00:01:44.061
On My results, he sees his best exam scores, his awareness band and his badges.

17
00:01:45.717 --> 00:01:51.944
When he passes a level, he gets a PDF certificate with a QR code that anyone can check.

18
00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:59.652
Next, Sione, a teacher, logs in.

19
00:02:00.783 --> 00:02:07.649
His dashboard shows his sections, finished exams, the average score, and families still to give consent.

20
00:02:08.817 --> 00:02:11.991
He can assign an exam to a class with one click.

21
00:02:13.617 --> 00:02:19.055
The class report lists every student by first name only, to protect privacy.

22
00:02:20.217 --> 00:02:25.504
He can download it as CSV or PDF, and all certificates as one ZIP file.

23
00:02:27.417 --> 00:02:31.705
AI only writes drafts. A teacher must approve each one.

24
00:02:32.783 --> 00:02:38.697
Māori content also needs approval from our cultural adviser, the Kaiārahi.

25
00:02:39.883 --> 00:02:45.135
This demo uses the free offline helper, so it works with no AI key at all.

26
00:02:49.883 --> 00:02:53.579
Now the School Admin of Bright Star School logs in.

27
00:02:54.683 --> 00:02:59.424
She sees the school licence: a Basic plan, and how many days are left.

28
00:03:00.583 --> 00:03:05.289
Level Packs show which levels the school owns, and the price of the others.

29
00:03:07.017 --> 00:03:11.990
Classes are split into sections, with up to 35 students in each section.

30
00:03:13.617 --> 00:03:19.450
To renew, the school types a product key. The key is signed, so it works even with no internet.

31
00:03:24.017 --> 00:03:27.481
Finally, the Super Admin runs the whole platform.

32
00:03:28.550 --> 00:03:34.266
The dashboard shows schools, students, exams, the pass rate and monthly income.

33
00:03:35.517 --> 00:03:39.701
Two payslips are waiting for review, and five help tickets are open.

34
00:03:42.350 --> 00:03:47.614
Business intelligence shows exams per month and the mix of licence plans.

35
00:03:48.750 --> 00:03:53.921
It also lists the weakest categories first, so we know which topics to improve.

36
00:03:55.583 --> 00:03:59.361
Schools pay by bank transfer and upload a payslip.

37
00:04:00.483 --> 00:04:06.583
The Super Admin checks it and approves it. The plan switches on, and a GST receipt is made.

38
00:04:08.217 --> 00:04:12.796
The help desk uses tickets with clear states, from open to closed.

39
00:04:14.517 --> 00:04:20.152
The security log records every login, failed login, lockout and Login as.

40
00:04:21.217 --> 00:04:26.051
After five wrong passwords, the account is locked for fifteen minutes.

41
00:04:27.817 --> 00:04:31.618
API keys are stored encrypted and shown masked.

42
00:04:32.683 --> 00:04:38.190
The offline helper means CyberQuest still works with no keys and no internet.

43
00:04:39.950 --> 00:04:45.051
User management supports two-step login, and every Login as is recorded.

44
00:04:46.750 --> 00:04:52.768
Help is on every page. The Explain this page button tells new users what each screen does.

45
00:04:54.550 --> 00:05:01.126
The panel explains the screen, and users can ask a question about it. If they are still stuck, they open a ticket.

46
00:05:02.383 --> 00:05:06.706
The health check confirms the app and the database are working.

47
00:05:07.483 --> 00:05:11.191
Our start script waits for this check before it opens the browser.

48
00:05:12.783 --> 00:05:17.826
CyberQuest. Learn. Play. Decide. Stay Cyber Safe. Thank you for watching.
